Uplink Port vs. Normal (Downlink) Port:
Feature	                              Uplink Port	                                                                                  Normal / Downlink Port
Primary Destination	                  Connected to a higher-layer network device (e.g., core switch, router).	                      Connected to local end-user devices (e.g., PCs, printers).
Traffic Handling	                    Aggregates and funnels massive amounts of outbound network traffic.	                          Handles single-device local segment traffic.
Common Hardware	                      Typically SFP+, SFP28, or QSFP fiber interfaces.	                                            Typically standard RJ45 Ethernet ports.

